      "text": "Here\u0027s a thinking process to analyze the provided registration form and translate its sections into requirements for the app\u0027s digital registration form, including multi-owner support:\n\n1.  **Understand the Goal:** The user wants to create a digital registration form within their app based on the provided physical PNG Small Craft Registration form. Key requirements are to identify all relevant data fields and ensure the app can handle multiple owners.\n\n2.  **Analyze the Form Structure:** Break down the physical form into logical sections.\n    *   Header: Title, Act Reference, Penalty Clause, SCA REGO No.\n    *   Office Use Only Section: Internal tracking numbers and flags.\n    *   Section A: Registration Type (New/Renewal).\n    *   Section B: Owner\u0027s Information.\n    *   Section C: Boat/Small Craft Details.\n    *   Section D: Registration Fee and Signatures (including payment details and declaration).\n    *   Footer: Print information.\n\n3.  **Map Form Fields to App Fields (Initial Pass - Section by Section):** Go through each field on the form and determine how it should be represented in the app.\n\n    *   **Header:**\n        *   `SCA REGO No.` (Top Right): This seems like a *final, assigned* registration number. The app should generate/assign this upon *successful* registration. It shouldn\u0027t be filled in *during* the initial application input by the user, but might be displayed later.\n        *   `APPLICATION FOR SMALL CRAFT REGISTRATION` / `PAPUA NEW GUINEA SMALL CRAFT ACT 2011` / Penalty Clause: These are informational and don\u0027t need direct data entry fields, but the context (e.g., associating the registration with this Act) is important for the app\u0027s purpose.\n\n    *   **Office Use ONLY:** These fields are *crucial* for internal processing and tracking *after* the application is submitted.\n        *   `Registration System ID`: The app\u0027s *internal* unique identifier for this registration record. Auto-generated.\n        *   `Interim Registration Number`: A temporary number assigned during processing. Needs a field.\n        *   `Safety Certificate Number`: Related to safety inspection/certification. Needs a field.\n        *   `Province of Registration`: Where the registration is being processed/filed. Needs a dropdown or text field.\n        *   `Method of Payment`: Link to payment info (see Section D). Probably a dropdown/radio button (Cash, Card, Bank Deposit).\n        *   `Safety Equipment Issued (Yes/No)`: Boolean/Checkbox/Radio Button.\n        *   `Payment Receipt Number`: Text field.\n        *   `Safety Equipment Issued Receipt Number`: Text field.\n        *   *App Context:* These fields would likely be filled in by a `Registrar` or `Administrator` role *after* the initial submission, not by the applicant.\n\n    *   **Section A: REGISTRATION:**\n        *   `NEW REGISTRATION ( ) / REGISTRATION RENEWAL ( )`: This is a key choice. In the app, this should be a clear selection (e.g., Radio buttons, dropdown) determining the workflow. If \u0027Renewal\u0027, the app might need to link to a previous registration record (e.g., require the existing SCA REGO No.).\n        *   *App Context:* This selection should likely be the first thing the user chooses when starting a registration.\n\n    *   **Section B: OWNER\u0027S INFORMATION:** This is the core owner data.\n        *   `NAME` (SURNAME, FIRST): Separate fields for first and last name.\n        *   `DATE OF BIRTH (dd/mm/yyyy)`: Date field with validation.\n        *   `AGE`: Can be auto-calculated from DOB or entered separately. Auto-calculation is better for data integrity.\n        *   `SEX`: Dropdown/Radio buttons (Male, Female, Other/Prefer not to say - consider modern practices).\n        *   `POSTAL`: Text field (can be multi-line or separate fields for Box No., etc.).\n        *   `ADDRESS` (TOWN/DISTRICT, LLG, WARD/VILLAGE): Separate text fields. Consider using dropdowns for standardized locations (Province, District, LLG, Ward) if possible, maybe populated by Admin.\n        *   `PHONE`: Text field (consider formatting/validation for phone numbers).\n        *   `FAX`: Text field (less common now, but included on the form).\n        *   `EMAIL`: Text field (with email format validation).\n        *   `PROOF OF OWNERSHIP`: This isn\u0027t a field to *fill in* details directly, but rather *describes* the *type* of document. The app needs a mechanism to *upload* these documents (scan/photo of bill of sale, title, etc.) and maybe a text field to *describe* the uploaded document(s).\n\n    *   **Section C: BOAT/SMALL CRAFT DETAILS:** Core vessel information.\n        *   `MAKE OF BOAT`: Text field.\n        *   `LENGTH`: Number field (specify units - meters/feet?).\n        *   `MODEL`: Text field.\n        *   `COLOR`: Text field (consider allowing multiple colors or using a primary/secondary structure).\n        *   `YEAR`: Number field (4 digits).\n        *   `HULL ID No./SERIAL No.`: Text field. *Crucial unique identifier*.\n        *   `ANY OTHER DISTINGUISH MARKS OR FEATURES`: Multi-line text field.\n        *   `PROP (CIRCLE)`: Select one option (Inboard, Outboard, Both, Sail, Other). Radio buttons or Dropdown. Add a text field if \"Other\" is selected.\n        *   `HULL MAT (CIRCLE)`: Select one option (Wood, Fiberglass, Metal, Inflatable, Other). Radio buttons or Dropdown. Add a text field if \"Other\" is selected.\n        *   `CRAFT USE (CIRCLE)`: Select one option (Pleasure, Passenger, Fishing, Cargo, Other). Radio buttons or Dropdown. Add a text field if \"Other\" is selected.\n        *   `FUEL (CIRCLE)`: Select one option (Electric, Gasoline, Diesel, Other). Radio buttons or Dropdown. Add a text field if \"Other\" is selected.\n        *   `TYPE (CIRCLE)`: Select one option (Open Boat, Cabin Cruiser, Sailboat, PWC, Other). Radio buttons or Dropdown. Add a text field if \"Other\" is selected.\n        *   `Boat Registration Expires After 3 Years`: Informational text. The app needs logic to calculate and track the expiry date based on the registration approval date.\n\n    *   **Section D: REGISTRATION FEE AND SIGNATURES:** Payment and declaration.\n        *   `SCA REGO No.` (Bottom Right): Duplicate of the top right. Assigned *after* approval.\n        *   `INTERIM REGISTRATION No:` (Payment section): Duplicate of the \u0027Office Use Only\u0027 field. Filled internally.\n        *   `PAYMENT METHOD`: Select one (Cash, Card, Bank Deposit). Radio buttons or Dropdown. Matches the \u0027Office Use Only\u0027 field.\n        *   `CARD NUMBER`: Text field (Only show if \u0027Card\u0027 is selected. Consider PCI compliance - maybe don\u0027t store the full number, or use a secure payment gateway).\n        *   `BANK STAMP REF:`: Text field (Only show if \u0027Bank Deposit\u0027 is selected).\n        *   `AMOUNT (KINA)`: Number field for the fee paid.\n        *   `SIGNATURE OF CARD HOLDER`: If payment is by card. In an app, this might be replaced by confirmation from a payment gateway or a checkbox affirmation.\n        *   `I (WE) HEREBY SWEAR OR AFFIRM...`: Declaration text. App needs a checkbox: \"I agree to the declaration above\".\n        *   `SIGNATURE(S) OF CRAFT OWNER`: In the app, this would likely be replaced by the authenticated user\u0027s submission action or a digital signature capture if required/feasible.\n        *   `DATE`: Date field, likely auto-populated on submission.\n\n4.  **Address the Multi-Owner Requirement:** The current form (Section B) only has space for *one* owner. The app needs to handle multiple owners.\n    *   **Solution:** Modify the \"Owner\u0027s Information\" section. Instead of having fields directly on the main form, have a *list* or *repeating section* for owners.\n    *   The user should be able to click an \"Add Owner\" button.\n    *   Each owner added would have their *own* set of fields identical to Section B (Name, DOB, Sex, Address, Contact Info, Proof of Ownership upload specific to their claim if needed).\n    *   Designate one owner as the \"Primary Contact\" or \"Primary Owner\" for communication purposes.\n    *   The declaration needs to reflect multiple owners (\"We hereby swear...\" - which it already does). The digital agreement mechanism should cover all listed owners implicitly upon submission by the primary applicant, or potentially require separate logins/confirmations if high legal assurance is needed (though this adds complexity).\n\n5.  **Refine and Structure the App Form:** Organize the collected fields logically within the app interface. Group related fields together.\n\n    *   **Section 1: Registration Type:** (New / Renewal)\n    *   **Section 2: Owner Information:** (Allow adding multiple owners, each with fields from Section B. Mark one as primary). Add Proof of Ownership upload *per owner* or *per registration*. Per registration is simpler.\n    *   **Section 3: Craft Details:** (Fields from Section C).\n    *   **Section 4: Supporting Documents:** (Centralized place to upload Proof of Ownership, maybe other required docs).\n    *   **Section 5: Declaration:** (Text + Checkbox).\n    *   **Section 6: Payment Information (May be handled separately):** Payment details might be entered *after* initial submission or integrated via a payment gateway. The fields from Section D related to payment (Method, Amount, Ref#, Card#) would go here or in the \u0027Office Use Only\u0027 section if payment is handled offline/later.\n    *   **Section 7: Office Use / Internal Processing:** (Fields from \u0027Office Use Only\u0027 block + assigned SCA Rego No., Interim No.). This section is *not* visible/editable by the applicant but by internal staff (`Registrar`, `Admin`).\n\n6.  **Add App-Specific Fields/Metadata:** Include fields needed for app operation but not on the physical form.\n    *   `Record Created Date/Time`\n    *   `Created By User`\n    *   `Last Modified Date/Time`\n    *   `Last Modified By User`\n    *   `Registration Status` (e.g., Draft, Submitted, Under Review, Approved, Rejected, Expired) - Crucial for workflow.\n    *   `Expiry Date` (Calculated).\n    *   Link to related `Inspection Records`.\n\n7.  **Final Review:** Check against the original form and the multi-owner requirement. Ensure all necessary data capture points are included. Ensure clarity on which fields are for applicants vs. internal staff. Check data types (text, number, date, dropdown, checkbox, file upload).",
