      "text": "Okay, this is excellent information. Based on these three schedules, here\u0027s a *simple* inspection checklist structure suitable for your app. The idea is to hit the key, observable points. Inspectors can then add detailed notes or photos for specifics.\n\nFor the app, each item would ideally be a check (Yes/No/N/A) with an optional field for notes and photo upload.\n\n---\n\n**NCD Small Craft Inspection Checklist**\n\n**Inspector Name:** `_________________________`\n**Date of Inspection:** `_________________________`\n**Craft Registration No. (SCA REGO No.):** `_________________________`\n**Craft Hull ID No. / Serial No.:** `_________________________`\n**Craft Type (e.g., Open Dinghy, Commercial, Cabin Cruiser):** `_________________________`\n\n---\n\n**A. Marking and Load Line Requirements (Schedule 1)**\n\n| Item                                                                     | Yes | No  | N/A | Notes / Photo Ref. |\n| :----------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :----------------- |\n| **1. Registration Number Marking:**                                      |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Legibly \u0026 permanently printed on BOTH sides?                        |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Located approx. 120cm from bow center, near top of hull?            |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Letters/Numbers at least 10cm high?                                 |     |     |     |                    |\n|   d. Stroke of letters/numbers at least 2cm wide?                        |     |     |     |                    |\n| **2. Load Line Marking (if commercial/open craft):**                     |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Legibly \u0026 permanently marked on BOTH sides?                         |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Located at craft mid-length?                                        |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Is it a triangle shape?                                             |     |     |     |                    |\n|   d. Triangle approx. 100mm high?                                        |     |     |     |                    |\n|   e. Triangle base approx. 20mm?                                         |     |     |     |                    |\n|   f. Triangle inverted (point down)?                                     |     |     |     |                    |\n|   g. Point of triangle \u003e\u003d 300mm from top edge of hull?                   |     |     |     |                    |\n| **3. Exemption Notice Presented (if applicable)?**                       |     |     |     |                    |\n\n---\n\n**B. Safety Standards (Schedule 3)**\n\n*Note: Some items depend on craft type/operation.*\n\n| Item                                                                     | Yes | No  | N/A | Notes / Photo Ref. |\n| :----------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :----------------- |\n| **1. For ALL Registered Craft:**                                         |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. ISO 12402 compliant Lifejackets (sufficient for all persons, incl. children sizes)? |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Pair of oars or paddles?                                            |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Functioning waterproof torch?                                       |     |     |     |                    |\n|   d. Mirror or similar signalling device?                                |     |     |     |                    |\n|   e. Anchor with at least 20 meters of rope?                             |     |     |     |                    |\n|   f. Sea anchor/tarpaulin with deployment rope?                          |     |     |     |                    |\n|   g. Bucket or bailer?                                                   |     |     |     |                    |\n|   h. First aid kit present?                                              |     |     |     |                    |\n|   i. Fire extinguisher (if enclosed hull craft)?                         |     |     |     |                    |\n|   j. Engine (if fitted) appears maintained \u0026 functional?                 |     |     |     |                    |\n|   k. Basic engine tools/spares (e.g., sparkplug, tool if petrol engine)? |     |     |     |                    |\n|   l. Sail or tarpaulin (bright color) for alternative use?               |     |     |     |                    |\n|   m. Sufficient fuel observed for intended short journey/operation?      |     |     |     |                    |\n| **2. For Craft Traveling OUT OF SIGHT OF LAND:**                         |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Reliable compass OR mobile phone with emergency call capability?    |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Emergency food and water (sufficient for persons/24hrs)?            |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Reserve fuel supply (25% of journey needs)?                         |     |     |     |                    |\n| **3. For Craft Traveling AT NIGHT:**                                     |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Bright light(s) visible from all directions?                        |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Other navigation lights (as required/approved)?                     |     |     |     |                    |\n| **4. For COMMERCIAL Small Craft (Licensed):**                            |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Reliable compass OR GPS (device or phone)?                          |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Emergency food and water (sufficient for persons/24hrs)? (Covered above but confirm) |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Whistle or horn?                                                    |     |     |     |                    |\n| **5. Exemption Notice Presented (if applicable)?**                       |     |     |     |                    |\n\n---\n\n**C. Construction Standards (Schedule 2 - Simplified Visual Checks)**\n\n*Note: Many construction standards require detailed assessment or certification. This focuses on observable aspects.*\n\n| Item                                                                     | Yes | No  | N/A | Notes / Photo Ref. |\n| :----------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-- | :-- | :-- | :----------------- |\n| **1. General Condition:**                                                |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Hull appears sound, no obvious major damage/leaks?                  |     |     |     |                    |\n| **2. Builder\u0027s Plate (if fitted/required):**                             |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Builder\u0027s Plate visible and legible?                                |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Plate shows max power, load, persons capacity?                      |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Plate shows constructor\u0027s serial number \u0026 completion date?          |     |     |     |                    |\n| **3. Flotation \u0026 Buoyancy:**                                             |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Evidence of built-in flotation (material/air chambers)?             |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Air compartments (if used for buoyancy) marked with \"Caution...\" label? |     |     |     |                    |\n| **4. Hull Integrity \u0026 Fittings:**                                        |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Bilge pump functional OR bucket/bailer present?                     |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Drain plugs appear secure, in good condition, and lockable?         |     |     |     |                    |\n|   c. Deck surfaces intended for walking appear slip-resistant?           |     |     |     |                    |\n|   d. Toe rail or similar on outboard edges of deck?                      |     |     |     |                    |\n|   e. Transom appears sound and able to support engine?                   |     |     |     |                    |\n|   f. Motor well (if present) appears watertight to hull \u0026 drains properly? |     |     |     |                    |\n|   g. Hardware/fittings (cleats, etc.) secure, good condition, no sharp edges? |     |     |     |                    |\n|   h. Bow eye suitable for towing, secure, above waterline?               |     |     |     |                    |\n| **5. Visibility:**                                                       |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Sufficient area of hull painted NMSA approved marine orange?        |     |     |     |                    |\n| **6. Fire Safety (Enclosed / Inboard):**                                 |     |     |     |                    |\n|   a. Fire extinguisher(s) properly mounted \u0026 accessible? (If required by type) |     |     |     |                    |\n|   b. Discharge port for extinguisher into inboard engine compartment (if applicable)? |     |     |     |                    |\n| **7. Exemption Notice Presented (if applicable)?**                       |     |     |     |                    |\n| **8. Construction Certification Presented (if post Oct 2016 commercial)?** |     |     |     |                    |\n\n---\n\n**Overall Inspection Outcome:**\n( ) Pass\n( ) Pass with Recommendations\n( ) Fail (Specify critical items in notes)\n\n**Inspector Summary / Recommendations:**\n`__________________________________________________________________________________`\n`__________________________________________________________________________________`\n`__________________________________________________________________________________`\n\n**Inspector Signature:** `_________________________`\n\n---\n\n**Implementation Notes for the App:**\n\n*   **Dynamic Checklists:** Ideally, the app could tailor the checklist slightly based on the \"Craft Type\" selected at the beginning (e.g., automatically mark N/A for commercial-only items if it\u0027s a private pleasure craft).\n*   **Mandatory Fields:** Some initial fields (Rego No., Date) should be mandatory.\n*   **Photo Integration:** Each checklist item or section should allow easy photo uploads.\n*   **Notes Field:** Essential for inspectors to add specific details, measurements, or observations.\n*   **Save/Submit:** Ability to save a draft inspection and submit a final one.\n*   **PDF Generation:** The app should be able to generate a PDF of the completed inspection report.\n*   **Reference Linking:** The checklist templates in your `checklistTemplates` collection should be built from these items. The `inspections` collection would store the *results* of these checks for a specific craft.\n\nThis checklist provides a solid foundation for your inspection module. Remember to consult with NCD Small Crafts personnel or relevant authorities to ensure it aligns with their operational needs and interpretations of the schedules.",
