      "text": "**Designing the Operator Module**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on designing the \"Operator Licensing\" module. I\u0027m prioritizing the needs of commercial craft operations, ensuring it caters to Fishing, Passenger, Cargo, and Mixed Use businesses. My immediate goal is to establish a robust framework for handling licenses for both Captains and Crew. The Operator License Registration will be the foundation of this module.\n\n\n**Outlining Operator Data Structure**\n\nI\u0027m now detailing the Firestore structure for the new module. We\u0027ll have an `operatorLicenses` collection and a separate `operators` collection to hold personal information. The `operators` collection will include fields like `surname`, `firstName`, and `dob`, all essential for managing individual operator profiles. We also need to decide how to handle the connection with app users.\n\n\n**Developing License Statuses**\n\nI\u0027m now integrating the license statuses into the data structure. The new `operatorLicenses` collection will feature statuses like \"Draft,\" \"Submitted,\" and \"PendingReview\" to manage the license lifecycle. These statuses will drive the UI flows and workflows. The status field also includes entries for different workflow events, and I am still determining how to best handle them.\n\n\n**Constructing Data Structures**\n\nI\u0027m now focusing on defining the complete data structures, including the `operatorLicenses` and the new `operators` collection. The `operators` collection will contain detailed personal information (PII) of operators, and I am also considering the fields needed for the \u0027CompetencyTests\u0027 collection. I\u0027m aiming for a well-structured and extensible design.\n\n\n**Outlining Firestore Structure**\n\nI\u0027ve started sketching out the Firestore structure, primarily focusing on the `operatorLicenses` and the new `operators` collection. The `operators` collection will contain comprehensive Personally Identifiable Information (PII) of operators, and I am also considering the fields needed for the \u0027CompetencyTests\u0027 collection. I\u0027m aiming for a well-structured and extensible design.\n\n\n**Constructing the Module**\n\nI\u0027m now fully immersed in developing the new \"Operator Licensing\" module. I\u0027ve defined the complete Firestore data structure, including the `operatorLicenses`, `operators`, and `competencyTests` collections, and the `testTemplates` collection. I am now focused on crafting robust UI screens for operator registration, competency testing, and license management. My primary aim is to ensure all data is easily accessible and correctly linked. I\u0027ll need to start building logic into the UI screens as well.\n\n\n**Designing Data Relationships**\n\nI\u0027ve finalized the data structure for the module. I\u0027ve designed the `operatorLicenses`, `operators`, and `competencyTests` collections, and also defined the `testTemplates` collection. I am now working on connecting licensed operators to crafts in the existing `registrations` collection and building logic for the UI screens.\n\n\n**Establishing the Module Structure**\n\nI\u0027m now fully immersed in developing the new \"Operator Licensing\" module. I\u0027ve designed the `operatorLicenses`, `operators`, `competencyTests`, and `testTemplates` collections. I am now working on connecting licensed operators to crafts in the existing `registrations` collection and building logic for the UI screens.\n\n\n**Establishing the Operator Data Structure**\n\nNow I\u0027m designing the complete structure for the \"Operator Licensing\" module. I\u0027ve broken down the data into key sections: operator licenses, operators, competency tests, and test templates. My goal is to streamline the registration process and improve the data organization within the module. I\u0027m focusing on ensuring data integrity and simplifying the UI flow.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Relationships**\n\nI\u0027ve successfully linked licensed operators to commercial crafts within the `registrations` collection. I\u0027ve also incorporated the logic for the UI screens. I\u0027m confident in the structure for the \"Operator Licensing\" module and the related UI screens.\n\n\n**Developing Key Module Features**\n\nI\u0027m now detailing the database structure, specifically the `operatorLicenses`, `operators`, and `competencyTests` collections, and the `testTemplates` collection. I\u0027ve designed the UI screens for operator registration, competency testing, and license management. I\u0027m focusing on crafting and connecting the database to UI screens and implementing business logic.\n\n\n**Implementing Initial UI Screens**\n\nI\u0027m now fully immersed in developing the UI screens for the new module. I\u0027m prioritizing the Operator License List Screen, focusing on data filtering and display, and planning the Operator License Detail Screen and form. I\u0027m also preparing for the Competency Test Record Screen and UI logic.\n\n\n**Designing the Module**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on the `operatorLicenses`, `operators`, and `testTemplates` data structures, along with the UI screens for operator registration, competency testing, and license management. I\u0027m building screens for the operator licenses list and detail screen, and integrating the related workflows.\n\n\n",
