      "text": "Okay, here\u0027s the comprehensive plan for your NCD CraftTrack application, presented in a continuous text format:\n\n**App Concept: NCD CraftTrack**\n\nThe NCD CraftTrack application will serve as a comprehensive digital platform for the NCD Small Crafts authority. Its primary purpose is to manage the lifecycle of small crafts, encompassing their registration, regular inspections, and the licensing of operators, particularly for commercial vessels. The system will facilitate progress tracking for all these processes and will be equipped to generate various reports. A key feature will be multi-level login access, ensuring that users only have permissions relevant to their roles.\n\n**Firebase Backend Setup**\n\nTo power this application, we will leverage Firebase services. Firebase Authentication will be used, primarily with Email/Password sign-in for user access. Firestore Database will be the core data storage solution, housing all application data in a NoSQL, document-based structure. Firebase Storage will also be essential for handling file uploads, with dedicated folders for different types of files, such as `proof_of_ownership/`, `inspection_evidence/`, `registration_certificates/`, `operator_license_photos/`, and `operator_license_documents/`.\n\n**Firestore Database Collections and Data Structure**\n\nThe Firestore database will be organized into several collections:\n\n1.  **`users` Collection:** This collection will store information about each application user. The document ID will be the Firebase Authentication User UID. Each document will include `userId` (matching the Auth UID), `email` (from Auth), `displayName`, `role` (e.g., \"Admin\", \"Registrar\", \"Inspector\", \"Supervisor\", \"ReadOnly\", \"LicenseOfficer\"), `createdAt` (timestamp), and `isActive` (boolean for disabling access).\n\n2.  **`registrations` Collection:** This will hold all records pertaining to small craft registrations. Each document, with an auto-generated ID, will contain fields like `registrationId` (a copy of the document ID), `scaRegoNo` (the official registration number, assigned on approval), `interimRegoNo`, `registrationType` (\"New\" or \"Renewal\"), `previousScaRegoNo` (if renewing), `status` (tracking the registration lifecycle like \"Draft\", \"Submitted\", \"Approved\", etc.), various timestamps (`submittedAt`, `approvedAt`, `effectiveDate`, `expiryDate`), `provinceOfRegistration`, payment details (`paymentMethod`, `paymentReceiptNumber`, `bankStampRef`, `paymentAmount`, `paymentDate`), safety certification details (`safetyCertNumber`, `safetyEquipIssued`, `safetyEquipReceiptNumber`).\n    A crucial part will be the `owners` field, a list of maps, where each map represents an owner and includes `ownerId`, `role` (\"Primary\" or \"CoOwner\"), `surname`, `firstName`, `dob`, `sex`, contact details, and address components.\n    Another list of maps, `proofOfOwnershipDocs`, will store details of uploaded ownership documents (`docId`, `description`, `fileName`, `fileUrl`, `uploadedAt`).\n    Craft-specific details will include `craftMake`, `craftModel`, `craftYear`, `craftColor`, `hullIdNumber`, `craftLength` (with `lengthUnits`), `distinguishingFeatures`, `propulsionType` (with `propulsionOtherDesc`), `hullMaterial` (with `hullMaterialOtherDesc`), `craftUse` (e.g., \"Pleasure\", \"Passenger\", \"Fishing\", \"Cargo\", \"MixedCommercial\", with `craftUseOtherDesc`), `fuelType` (with `fuelTypeOtherDesc`), and `vesselType` (with `vesselTypeOtherDesc`).\n    Information about the generated registration certificate (`certificateGeneratedAt`, `certificateFileName`, `certificateFileUrl`) will also be stored.\n    For commercial crafts, an `assignedOperators` field (list of maps) will link to licensed operators, detailing their `operatorLicenseRef` and `roleOnCraft`.\n    Finally, audit fields like `lastUpdatedByRef` (a reference to the `users` collection), `lastUpdatedAt`, `createdByRef` (reference to `users`), and `createdAt` will be included.\n\n3.  **`inspections` Collection:** This will store records for every inspection conducted. Each document will have an `inspectionId`, a `registrationRef` (linking to the specific craft in the `registrations` collection), an `inspectorRef` (linking to the `users` collection), `inspectionType` (e.g., \"Initial\", \"AnnualSafety\", \"MarkingLoadline\"), `scheduledDate`, `inspectionDate`, `status` (e.g., \"Scheduled\", \"Completed\", \"Passed\"), `overallResult`, `findings` (summary notes), `correctiveActions`, and a `followUpRequired` boolean.\n    A `checklistItems` field (list of maps) will detail each item checked during the inspection, including `itemId` (from the template), `itemDescription`, `category`, `result` (\"Yes\", \"No\", \"Pass\", \"Fail\", \"N/A\"), `comments`, and `evidenceUrls` (list of photo URLs from Storage). Audit fields (`completedAt`, `createdAt`, `createdByRef`) will also be present.\n\n4.  **`checklistTemplates` Collection:** This admin-managed collection will hold reusable templates for inspections. Each template document will have a `templateId`, `name` (e.g., \"Schedule 1 - Marking and Load Line\"), `inspectionTypeAssociation` (to link with `inspections`), and an `items` field (list of maps). Each item map will define a checklist question with `itemId`, `itemDescription`, an optional `category`, and an `order` for display. `isActive`, `createdAt`, and `createdByRef` fields are also included.\n\n5.  **`operators` Collection:** This collection will store the personal details of individuals who apply for or hold operator licenses, separate from their license applications. Each document will have an `operatorId`, `surname`, `firstName`, `dob`, `age`, `sex`, detailed `placeOfOrigin` (Town, District, LLG, Village), `phoneMobile`, `email`, `postalAddress`, physical characteristics (`heightCm`, `eyeColor`, `skinColor`, `hairColor`, `weightKg`), `bodyMarks`, and an `idSizePhotoUrl` (link to Firebase Storage). Timestamps for `createdAt` and `updatedAt` will be maintained.\n\n6.  **`operatorLicenses` Collection:** This collection manages individual operator license applications and the issued licenses. Each document will have a `licenseApplicationId`, `assignedLicenseNumber` (official number), an `operatorRef` (linking to the `operators` collection), `licenseType` (\"Captain\" or \"Crew\"), `applicationType` (\"New\" or \"Renewal\"), `previousLicenseNumber` (if applicable), `status` (tracking the application lifecycle, e.g., \"Submitted\", \"AwaitingTest\", \"Approved\", \"Expired\"), various timestamps (`submittedAt`, `issuedAt`, `expiryDate`), `issuePlace`, payment details (`paymentMethod`, `paymentBy`, `paymentReceiptNo`).\n    An `attachedDocuments` field (list of maps) will store information about submitted documents like Police Clearance or NID Card, including `docType`, `fileName`, `fileUrl`, `uploadedAt`, and a `verified` flag for office use.\n    A `competencyTestRef` will link to the relevant test record. Audit fields include `lastUpdatedByRef`, `lastUpdatedAt`, `createdByUserRef`, and `createdAt`.\n\n7.  **`competencyTestTemplates` Collection:** Admin-managed templates for the competency tests required for operator licensing. Each template will have a `templateId`, `templateName`, `testVersion`, `description`, `licenseTypeEligibility`, a list of `questions` (each with `questionId`, `questionText`, `questionType` like \"MultipleChoice\", options, `correctAnswer`, and `points`), a `passingScorePercentage`, `isActive` status, and audit fields.\n\n8.  **`competencyTests` Collection:** Records of competency tests taken by operators. Each document will have a `testId`, `operatorRef`, `licenseApplicationRef`, `testTemplateRef`, `testDate`, `examinerRef` (the app user who administered it), `scoreAchieved`, `percentageAchieved`, `result` (\"Pass\" or \"Fail\"). An optional `answers` field (list of maps) can store detailed responses for review. `notes` by the examiner and `createdAt` timestamp are also included.\n\n**User Interface Screens and Workflows**\n\nThe application will be divided into several modules with distinct screens:\n\n*   **Authentication Module:** Will include a `LoginScreen` for email/password authentication and a `UserProfileScreen` for users to view and edit their basic profile information like display name.\n*   **Dashboard Module:** The `DashboardScreen` will serve as the main landing page after login, presenting a role-based overview with relevant statistics, quick links to common tasks, and alerts.\n*   **Craft Registration Module:**\n    *   `RegistrationListScreen`: Displays a list of all craft registrations, with search and filter capabilities. Users can tap an item to view details.\n    *   `RegistrationEditScreen`: A form for creating new craft registrations or editing existing ones. This will handle the input of all craft details, including the multi-owner information and uploading proof of ownership documents.\n    *   `RegistrationDetailScreen`: Shows a comprehensive view of a specific craft\u0027s registration data, including linked inspections, assigned commercial operators, and allows authorized users to manage the registration status (approve, reject) and generate/download the registration certificate.\n*   **Inspections Module:**\n    *   `InspectionListScreen`: Lists all inspections, allowing users to search and filter.\n    *   `InspectionEditScreen`: The interface for inspectors to fill out the digital inspection checklist based on a loaded template, record findings for each item, add comments, and upload photographic evidence.\n    *   `InspectionDetailScreen`: Displays the completed inspection report for a specific craft.\n*   **Operator Licensing Module:** This module is key for managing commercial operations.\n    *   `OperatorLicenseListScreen`: Shows a list of all operator license applications and issued licenses, with search and filter functionalities.\n    *   `OperatorLicenseEditScreen`: A form based on the provided \"APPLICATION FOR OPERATOR\u0027S LICENSE\" image, allowing for the creation of new license applications or editing existing ones. This includes inputting applicant details, physical characteristics, place of origin, and uploading required documents (Police Clearance, ID photo, Birth Certificate, NID card, previous license if renewing).\n    *   `OperatorLicenseDetailScreen`: Provides a detailed view of an operator\u0027s license application. Authorized personnel (e.g., \"LicenseOfficer\" or \"Admin\") can manage the application status, fill in \"Office Use ONLY\" fields like License Number and Receipt No upon approval, and link to or view competency test results.\n    *   `CompetencyTestRecordScreen`: A screen for examiners or authorized personnel to record the results of a competency test taken by an operator. This could also include functionality for administering a simple, pre-defined test within the app.\n    *   `CompetencyTestDetailScreen`: Displays the details and results of a specific competency test.\n    *   `Admin_TestTemplateManagementScreen`: An admin-only screen for creating, reading, updating, and deleting competency test templates.\n*   **Reporting Module:**\n    *   `ReportGenerationScreen`: Allows users with appropriate permissions to select from a list of pre-defined report types, apply filters (e.g., date range, status), and then view or export the generated report (e.g., as PDF or CSV).\n*   **Admin Module:**\n    *   `UserManagementScreen`: For administrators to create, view, edit, and manage user accounts, including assigning roles and deactivating users.\n    *   `SettingsScreen`: For administrators to manage system-wide settings, such as inspection checklist templates and potentially other configurable parameters.\n\n**Reporting Capabilities**\n\nThe application will be designed to produce a range of reports, including but not limited to:\n\n*   A list of all Registered Crafts, filterable by status, type, owner, or location.\n*   Reports on Upcoming or Overdue Inspections.\n*   An Inspection Results Summary, showing pass/fail rates and identifying common deficiencies.\n*   A Craft Compliance Status report.\n*   Activity reports for Registrars and Inspectors.\n*   A report on Expiring Craft Registrations.\n*   A list of all Licensed Operators, filterable by license type, status, or expiry date.\n*   A report detailing Operator Licenses that are due for renewal.\n*   A summary of Competency Test Results.\n\nThis comprehensive plan provides a solid foundation for developing the NCD CraftTrack application, ensuring all specified requirements for registration, inspection, operator licensing, progress tracking, and reporting are met with appropriate role-based access controls.",
