      "text": "Okay, here\u0027s a focused breakdown specifically for the **Operator Licensing Module**, designed to manage licensing for commercial operations (Fishing, Passenger, Cargo, Mixed Use) for both Captains and Crew, incorporating the provided application form and the need for competency testing.\n\n**Operator Licensing Module**\n\nThis module is dedicated to managing the entire lifecycle of operator licenses, crucial for individuals captaining or crewing commercial small crafts. It will handle applications, document verification, competency testing, and license issuance and tracking.\n\n**Core Goals of the Licensing Module:**\n\n*   Digitize the \"APPLICATION FOR OPERATOR\u0027S LICENSE\" process.\n*   Maintain a database of licensed operators and their qualifications.\n*   Facilitate and record competency tests.\n*   Track license statuses, expiry, and renewals.\n*   Link licensed operators to relevant commercial craft registrations.\n\n**Firebase Data Structures for Licensing:**\n\n1.  **`operators` Collection:**\n    *   **Purpose:** Stores the enduring personal details of individuals who apply for or hold licenses. This creates a central record for each person, even if they apply for multiple licenses or renew over time.\n    *   **Key Fields (derived from form and needs):**\n        *   `operatorId` (Auto-generated Unique ID)\n        *   `surname`, `firstName`\n        *   `dob` (Date of Birth), `age`, `sex`\n        *   `placeOfOriginTown`, `placeOfOriginDistrict`, `placeOfOriginLLG`, `placeOfOriginVillage`\n        *   `phoneMobile`, `email`\n        *   `postalAddress`\n        *   `heightCm`, `eyeColor`, `skinColor`, `hairColor`, `weightKg`\n        *   `bodyMarks` (e.g., tattoo; scar etc.)\n        *   `idSizePhotoUrl` (Link to uploaded ID photo in Firebase Storage)\n        *   `createdAt`, `updatedAt`\n\n2.  **`operatorLicenses` Collection:**\n    *   **Purpose:** Manages each specific license application and the resulting license if approved.\n    *   **Key Fields:**\n        *   `licenseApplicationId` (Auto-generated Unique ID)\n        *   `operatorRef` (Reference to the relevant document in the `operators` collection)\n        *   `applicationType`: \"New\" or \"Renewal\"\n        *   `previousLicenseNumber` (If `applicationType` is \"Renewal\")\n        *   `status`: \"Draft\", \"Submitted\", \"PendingReview\", \"RequiresInfo\", \"AwaitingTest\", \"TestScheduled\", \"TestPassed\", \"TestFailed\", \"Approved\", \"Rejected\", \"Expired\", \"Revoked\"\n        *   `submittedAt`, `approvedAt`, `issuedAt`, `expiryDate`\n        *   **Office Use Only Fields (editable by authorized staff):**\n            *   `assignedLicenseNumber` (The official license number once issued)\n            *   `receiptNo`\n            *   `placeIssued`\n            *   `methodOfPayment`\n            *   `paymentBy`\n        *   **Attached Documents (List of Maps):** For each document from the form\u0027s checklist:\n            *   `docType`: \"PoliceClearance\", \"PreviousLicenseCopy\", \"BirthCertificateCopy\", \"NIDCardCopy\", \"Other\"\n            *   `fileName`, `fileUrl` (Link to Firebase Storage)\n            *   `uploadedAt`, `verifiedStatus` (\"Pending\", \"Verified\", \"Rejected\")\n        *   `competencyTestRef` (Reference to the `competencyTests` collection document)\n        *   `createdByUserRef`, `lastUpdatedByRef`, `createdAt`, `lastUpdatedAt`\n\n3.  **`competencyTestTemplates` Collection:**\n    *   **Purpose:** Stores reusable templates for different types or levels of competency tests.\n    *   **Key Fields:**\n        *   `templateId`, `templateName`, `description`\n        *   `applicableLicenseType`: \"Captain\", \"Crew\", \"GeneralCommercial\"\n        *   `questions` (List of Maps: `questionId`, `questionText`, `questionType` [\"MultipleChoice\", \"TrueFalse\"], `options`, `correctAnswer`, `points`)\n        *   `passingScorePercentage`\n        *   `isActive`, `createdAt`, `createdByRef`\n\n4.  **`competencyTests` Collection:**\n    *   **Purpose:** Records the details and results of each competency test taken by an operator.\n    *   **Key Fields:**\n        *   `testId`\n        *   `licenseApplicationRef` (Link to the specific license application)\n        *   `operatorRef` (Link to the operator who took the test)\n        *   `testTemplateRef` (Link to the template used)\n        *   `testDate`, `examinerRef` (User who administered/graded)\n        *   `scoreAchieved`, `percentageAchieved`, `result` (\"Pass\", \"Fail\")\n        *   `answers` (Optional: List of Maps: `questionId`, `answerGiven`, `isCorrect` for detailed review)\n        *   `notes` (Examiner\u0027s comments)\n        *   `createdAt`\n\n**UI Screens and Workflow for the Licensing Module:**\n\n1.  **Operator License List Screen (`OperatorLicenseListScreen`):**\n    *   **Display:** A table or list of all operator license applications and issued licenses.\n    *   **Information Shown:** Applicant Name, License Number (if issued), Application Type, Status, Submission Date, Expiry Date (if issued).\n    *   **Functionality:**\n        *   Search by applicant name, license number, status.\n        *   Filter by status, application type, expiry period.\n        *   \"Add New License Application\" button (navigates to `OperatorLicenseEditScreen`).\n        *   Clicking an item navigates to `OperatorLicenseDetailScreen`.\n\n2.  **Operator License Application/Edit Screen (`OperatorLicenseEditScreen`):**\n    *   **Purpose:** For creating a new license application or editing an existing one (if status allows). This screen will digitally mirror the provided \"APPLICATION FOR OPERATOR\u0027S LICENSE\" form.\n    *   **Sections \u0026 Fields:**\n        *   **Application Type:** Radio buttons for \"New\" / \"Renewal\". If \"Renewal\", a field for `previousLicenseNumber` appears.\n        *   **Applicant Information (Links to/Creates `operators` record):**\n            *   `Surname`, `First Name`\n            *   `Date of Birth` (Date picker), `Age` (auto-calculated or manual), `Sex` (Dropdown)\n        *   **Place of Origin:** `Town`, `District`, `LLG`, `Village`\n        *   **Contact:** `Phone (Mobile)`, `Email`\n        *   **Postal Address:** Text area.\n        *   **Physical Characteristics:** `Height (cm)`, `Colour of Eye`, `Color of Skin`, `Color of Hair`, `Weight (kg)`\n        *   **Any body marks:** `eg: tatoo ; scar etc..` (Text area)\n        *   **ID Size Photo Upload:** File upload component (stores to `operators.idSizePhotoUrl` and a copy to `operatorLicenses.attachedDocuments` with type \"IDPhoto\").\n        *   **Document Attachment Checklist:**\n            *   A section for each required document:\n                1.  Police Clearance\n                2.  Copy of Operator\u0027s License (if re-newing)\n                3.  Copy of Birth Certificate\n                4.  Copy of NID Card\n            *   Each item will have a file upload button and display the uploaded file\u0027s name/status. These link to the `operatorLicenses.attachedDocuments` list.\n    *   **Actions:**\n        *   \"Save Draft\" button.\n        *   \"Submit Application\" button (changes status to \"Submitted\").\n\n3.  **Operator License Detail Screen (`OperatorLicenseDetailScreen`):**\n    *   **Purpose:** To view all details of a submitted application or an issued license and manage its progression.\n    *   **Display:**\n        *   All information entered on the `OperatorLicenseEditScreen`, clearly laid out.\n        *   Status of attached documents (e.g., \"Pending Verification\", \"Verified\").\n        *   Link to view/manage competency test (`CompetencyTestDetailScreen` or link to schedule).\n    *   **\"Office Use ONLY\" Section (Editable by authorized roles like \"LicenseOfficer\" or \"Admin\"):**\n        *   `License Number` (input field, becomes read-only after initial save)\n        *   `Receipt No`\n        *   `Place Issued`\n        *   `Method of Payment`\n        *   `Payment By`\n        *   Fields for `issuedAt` (Date picker) and `expiryDate` (Date picker, potentially auto-calculated).\n    *   **Actions (Role-based and Status-dependent):**\n        *   **Verify Documents:** Checkbox/button next to each uploaded document for staff to mark as verified.\n        *   **Request More Information:** Change status to \"RequiresInfo\" and add a note for the applicant/internal staff.\n        *   **Schedule/Record Competency Test:** Button to navigate to `CompetencyTestRecordScreen` or link an existing test.\n        *   **Approve License:** (Available if documents verified and test passed) Staff input \"Office Use Only\" details, set `issuedAt` and `expiryDate`, change status to \"Approved\".\n        *   **Reject Application:** Change status to \"Rejected\" with a reason.\n        *   **Generate License Card (Placeholder):** Button to indicate a physical card would be produced (future: could generate a digital representation).\n\n4.  **Competency Test Management Screens:**\n    *   **Admin - Test Template Management Screen (`Admin_TestTemplateManagementScreen`):**\n        *   Admins can create new test templates (define questions, answers, type, points, passing score).\n        *   View, edit, and deactivate existing templates.\n    *   **Competency Test Record Screen (`CompetencyTestRecordScreen`):**\n        *   **Purpose:** For an examiner or authorized user to administer or record the results of a competency test for an applicant.\n        *   **Functionality:**\n            *   Select the applicant/license application.\n            *   Select the appropriate `competencyTestTemplate`.\n            *   **Option A (Simple Record):** Fields to manually enter `testDate`, `scoreAchieved`, `result` (\"Pass\"/\"Fail\"), and `examinerNotes`.\n            *   **Option B (Basic In-App Test):** Display questions from the selected template one by one or as a list. Operator/Examiner inputs answers. System auto-grades (if multiple choice/true-false) or allows examiner to mark short answers. Calculates score and determines Pass/Fail.\n        *   Save test results (creates/updates a document in `competencyTests` and updates `operatorLicenses.competencyTestRef` and potentially status).\n    *   **Competency Test Detail Screen (`CompetencyTestDetailScreen`):**\n        *   Displays the detailed results of a specific test taken by an operator, including answers if recorded.\n\n**Workflow for Commercial Craft Licensing:**\n\n1.  An individual (or an NCD staff member on their behalf) fills out the `OperatorLicenseEditScreen`.\n2.  Required documents and ID photo are uploaded. Application is submitted.\n3.  NCD staff (License Officer/Admin) reviews the application on `OperatorLicenseDetailScreen`, verifies documents.\n4.  If documents are okay, a competency test is scheduled/administered. Results are recorded via `CompetencyTestRecordScreen`.\n5.  If the test is passed and all other requirements are met, the License Officer/Admin uses the \"Office Use ONLY\" section on `OperatorLicenseDetailScreen` to input final details (License No., payment, issue/expiry dates) and approves the license.\n6.  The `assignedLicenseNumber`, `issuedAt`, and `expiryDate` are now official.\n7.  This licensed operator can then be linked to one or more commercial craft in the `registrations` collection (via the `registrations.assignedOperators` field).\n\nThis detailed structure for the Operator Licensing module will provide a robust system for managing commercial craft operator qualifications, ensuring compliance and safety.",
